{
  "id": "1CH.4",
  "number": "4",
  "bookId": "1CH",
  "reference": "1 Chronicles 4",
  "verseCount": 37,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "4",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "1CH 4"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "4",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "These are some of the descendants of Judah: Perez, Hezron, Carmi, Hur, and Shobal. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Shobal was the father of Reaiah, who was the father of Jahath, the father of Ahumai and Lahad, the ancestors of the people who lived in Zorah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.2"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hur was the eldest son of his father Caleb's wife Ephrath, and his descendants founded the city of Bethlehem. Hur had three sons: Etam, Penuel, and Ezer. Etam had three sons:",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.3+1CH.4.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.3",
              "1CH.4.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.3–4",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Some ancient translations",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "sons",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "fathers.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " Jezreel, Ishma, and Idbash, and one daughter, Hazzelelponi. Penuel founded the city of Gedor, and Ezer founded Hushah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.3+1CH.4.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.3",
              "1CH.4.4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.3+1CH.4.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.3",
              "1CH.4.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ashhur, who founded the town of Tekoa, had two wives, Helah and Naarah. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He and Naarah had four sons: Ahuzzam, Hepher, Temeni, and Haahashtari. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ashhur and Helah had three sons: Zereth, Izhar, and Ethnan.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.7"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Koz was the father of Anub and Zobebah, and the ancestor of the clans descended from Aharhel son of Harum.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.8"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There was a man named Jabez, who was the most respected member of his family. His mother had given him the name Jabez,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.9",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Jabez",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": ": This name sounds like the Hebrew for “pain”.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " because his birth had been very painful. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But Jabez prayed to the God of Israel, “Bless me, God, and give me much land. Be with me and keep me from anything evil that might cause me pain.” And God gave him what he prayed for.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.10"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Caleb, the brother of Shuhah, had a son, Mehir. Mehir was the father of Eshton, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "who had three sons: Bethrapha, Paseah, and Tehinnah. Tehinnah was the founder of the city of Nahash. The descendants of these men lived in Recah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Kenaz had two sons, Othniel and Seraiah. Othniel also had two sons, Hathath and Meonothai.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.13",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Some ancient translations",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Meonothai",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew does not have this name.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Meonothai was the father of Ophrah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Seraiah was the father of Joab, the founder of the Valley of Craftsmen, where all the people were skilled workmen.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Caleb son of Jephunneh had three sons: Iru, Elah, and Naam. And Elah was the father of Kenaz.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.15"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jehallelel had four sons: Ziph, Ziphah, Tiria, and Asarel.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ezrah had four sons: Jether, Mered, Epher, and Jalon. Mered married Bithiah, a daughter of the king of Egypt, and they had a daughter, Miriam, and two sons, Shammai and Ishbah. Ishbah founded the town of Eshtemoa. Mered also married a woman from the tribe of Judah, and they had three sons: Jered, who founded the town of Gedor; Heber, founder of the town of Soco; and Jekuthiel, founder of the town of Zanoah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.17+1CH.4.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.17",
              "1CH.4.18"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.17+1CH.4.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.17",
              "1CH.4.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hodiah married the sister of Naham. Their descendants founded the clan of Garm, which lived in the town of Keilah, and the clan of Maacath, which lived in the town of Eshtemoa.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.19",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Verse 19 in Hebrew is unclear.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Shimon had four sons: Amnon, Rinnah, Benhanan, and Tilon.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.20"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ishi had two sons: Zoheth and Benzoheth.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.20"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Shelah was one of Judah's sons. His descendants included Er, who founded the town of Lecah; Laadah, founder of the town of Mareshah; the clan of linen weavers, who lived in the town of Beth Ashbea; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jokim and the people who lived in the town of Cozeba; and Joash and Saraph, who married Moabite women and then settled in Bethlehem.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.22",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Probable text",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "settled in Bethlehem",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew unclear.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " (These traditions are very old.) ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They were potters in the service of the king and lived in the towns of Netaim and Gederah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Simeon had five sons: Nemuel, Jamin, Jarib, Zerah, and Shaul. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Shaul's son was Shallum, his grandson was Mibsam, and his great-grandson was Mishma. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then from Mishma the line descended through Hammuel, Zaccur, and Shimei. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Shimei had sixteen sons and six daughters, but his relatives had fewer children, and the tribe of Simeon did not grow as much as the tribe of Judah did.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.27"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.27"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "28",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:28"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "28",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "JOS.19.2+JOS.19.3+JOS.19.4+JOS.19.5+JOS.19.6+JOS.19.7+JOS.19.8"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Josh 19.2–8",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "\n",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Down to the time of King David the descendants of Simeon lived in the following towns: Beersheba, Moladah, Hazarshual, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.28",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.28"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "29",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:29"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "29",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bilhah, Ezem, Tolad, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.29",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.29"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "30",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:30"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "30",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bethuel, Hormah, Ziklag, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.30",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.30"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "31",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:31"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "31",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Beth Marcaboth, Hazarsusim, Bethbiri, and Shaaraim. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.31",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.31"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "32",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:32"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "32",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They also lived in five other places: Etam, Ain, Rimmon, Tochen, and Ashan, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.32",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.32"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and the surrounding villages, as far south-west as the town of Baalath. These are the records which they kept of their families and of the places where they lived.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.33"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "33",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:33"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "33",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.33",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.33"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The following men were the heads of their clans:",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.34+1CH.4.35+1CH.4.36+1CH.4.37+1CH.4.38",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.34",
              "1CH.4.35",
              "1CH.4.36",
              "1CH.4.37",
              "1CH.4.38"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "34",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:34"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "34",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because their families continued to grow, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.34+1CH.4.35+1CH.4.36+1CH.4.37+1CH.4.38",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.34",
              "1CH.4.35",
              "1CH.4.36",
              "1CH.4.37",
              "1CH.4.38"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "39",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:39"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "39",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "they spread out westwards almost to Gerar",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.39",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.39"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.39",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Some ancient translations",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gerar",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gedor.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " and pastured their sheep on the eastern side of the valley in which that city is located. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.39",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.39"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "40",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:40"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "40",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They found plenty of fertile pasture lands there in a stretch of open country that was quiet and peaceful. The people who had lived there before were Hamites.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.40",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.40"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "40",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:40"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "40",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.40",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.40"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "41",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:41"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "41",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the time of King Hezekiah of Judah, the men named above went to Gerar and destroyed the tents and huts of the people who lived there.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.41",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.41"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4.41",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the tents and huts",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "…",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "there",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; or",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "the tents of the people who lived there, and the Meunites also.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " They drove the people out and settled there permanently because there was plenty of pasture for their sheep. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.41",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.41"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "42",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:42"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "42",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "500 other members of the tribe of Simeon went east to Edom. They were led by the sons of Ishi: Pelatiah, Neariah, Rephaiah, and Uzziel. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.42",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.42"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "43",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "1CH 4:43"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "43",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There they killed the surviving Amalekites, and they have lived there ever since.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "1CH.4.43",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "1CH.4.43"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
